<!-- Secção Context -->
<section class="section-light" id="context">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Context</h2>
        <p class="project-intro">
            The Brainstorm PHDA website was designed for a diverse audience connected to ADHD, including individuals
            diagnosed with the condition, families, caregivers, educators and healthcare professionals.
        </p>
        <p class="project-intro">
            The platform acts as a central hub, providing access to reliable information, support resources and
            community initiatives, while helping to reduce misconceptions around ADHD and strengthen awareness
            at a national level.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Secção Challenge -->
<section class="section" id="challenge">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Challenge</h2>
        <p class="project-intro">
            Designing for this audience required a careful balance between clarity, accessibility and emotional sensitivity.
            Given the user profile — particularly individuals with ADHD — it was essential to account for shorter attention
            spans, sensitivity to stimuli and cognitive overload.
        </p>
        <p class="project-intro">
            The challenge was to create a clear and intuitive experience that simplifies access to information, supports
            different user journeys, and remains engaging without overwhelming the user. This meant prioritising
            straightforward navigation, reducing friction, and applying accessibility and usability principles throughout
            the entire experience.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Secção Objetivos -->
<section class="section-light" id="goals">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Goals</h2>
        <div class="project-grid">
            <div class="project-card-box">
                <h3>Establish Trust and Authority</h3>
                <p>
                    Position the platform as a trusted, authoritative source of ADHD information in Portugal,
                    providing reliable and evidence-based resources for all users.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-card-box">
                <h3>Meet Accessibility Standards</h3>
                <p>
                    Ensure WCAG 2.1 AA compliance across all interactive elements, making the platform
                    usable for people with varying abilities and assistive technology users.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-card-box">
                <h3>Improve Information Discoverability</h3>
                <p>
                    Enhance content findability through clear navigation and structured content architecture
                    that helps users locate what they need quickly and efficiently.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-card-box">
                <h3>Reduce Cognitive Load</h3>
                <p>
                    Minimise mental effort through scaffolded content, adjustable complexity, and thoughtful
                    interface design that respects neurodivergent user needs.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Secção Processo -->
<section class="section" id="process">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Process</h2>
        <div class="project-grid">
            <div class="process-steps">
                <div class="process-item">
                    <div class="process-number">1</div>
                    <div class="process-content">
                        <h3>Discover — User and Domain Research</h3>
                        <p>
                            Conducted user interviews with individuals with ADHD, families, and healthcare professionals,
                            alongside stakeholder alignment sessions and review of ADHD-related literature to understand
                            behaviours, needs and pain points.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="process-item">
                    <div class="process-number">2</div>
                    <div class="process-content">
                        <h3>Define — Problem Framing and Structure</h3>
                        <p>
                            Synthesised research insights into key challenges, defined user needs, and created
                            a comprehensive information architecture and sitemap to support different user journeys
                            and content types.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="process-item">
                    <div class="process-number">3</div>
                    <div class="process-content">
                        <h3>Develop — Design Exploration and Validation</h3>
                        <p>
                            Created wireframes and high-fidelity UI designs focused on clarity and accessibility,
                            with iterative usability testing to refine navigation patterns and interaction design
                            for neurodivergent users.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="process-item">
                    <div class="process-number">4</div>
                    <div class="process-content">
                        <h3>Deliver — Implementation and Optimisation</h3>
                        <p>
                            Delivered final UI designs with comprehensive documentation, supported developer handoff,
                            and conducted usability validation to ensure a consistent, accessible and scalable experience.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Secção Wireframes -->
<section class="section-light" id="wireframes">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Wireframes</h2>
        <p class="project-intro-centered">
            Early wireframes focused on creating a clean, distraction-free layout that reduces cognitive load
            and supports clear information hierarchy for users with ADHD.
        </p>
        <div class="project-grid">
            <div class="wireframe-section">
                <h3>Desktop Wireframes</h3>
                <img src="img/projects/brainstorm/wireframe-desktop.png"
                     srcset="img/projects/brainstorm/wireframe-desktop.png 1x, img/projects/brainstorm/wireframe-desktop@2x.png 2x"
                     alt="Desktop wireframes for Brainstorm PHDA platform">
            </div>
            <div class="wireframe-section">
                <h3>Desktop Wireframes — Alternative Layout</h3>
                <img src="img/projects/brainstorm/wireframe-desktop-2.png"
                     srcset="img/projects/brainstorm/wireframe-desktop-2.png 1x, img/projects/brainstorm/wireframe-desktop-2@2x.png 2x"
                     alt="Alternative desktop wireframes for Brainstorm PHDA">
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

